# The read that finds an expired cache entry tells the host, during the
# assert ([NSTG.2.4.2]).
#
# Pump 1    `rw` writes "k" with a 10_s TTL.
# Advance   to exactly the deadline, with no pump, so no sweep has run.
# Assert q  `rq1`'s and `rq2`'s join tests read `cached("k")`; the first read
#           evicts it and tells the host, once.
#
# No pump follows the last assert, so the notification can come only from
# the read.
assert Trig tag=w
pump
advance 10000000000
assert Trig tag=q
